            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How does S. Phaneuf & Associates manage high groundwater during site excavation in Littleton, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates installs temporary dewatering pump systems and digs peripheral interceptor drainage trenches to control high groundwater common in Littleton. Crews backfill excavated foundation sites with washed 3/4-inch crushed stone and install heavy perforated filter-fabric drain pipes connected to drywells or catch basins. This engineering keeps foundation footings dry and prevents subgrade saturation prior to pouring concrete or paving asphalt.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: What is the benefit of installing Cape Cod berms on Littleton, MA driveways?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates installs extruded asphalt Cape Cod berms along driveway borders to direct surface stormwater runoff into designated drainage areas. Cape Cod berms prevent rainwater from washing away topsoil, protect lawn edges from vehicle tire damage, and reinforce the structural edge of the asphalt driveway against cracking during winter freezing and snowplow operations in Littleton.</p>
